X: 1
T: Lord As To Thy Dear Cross
C: Words: John Hampden Gurney, 1838.
C: Music: 'St. Bernard (Richardson)' or 'St. Bernard (Tochter Sion)' from Tochter Sion, Cologne, 1741.
C: Setting: John Richardson, 1877.
C: copyright: public domain.  This score is a part of the Open Hymnal Project, 2026 Revision.
S: Music and Lyrics source: "The New Hymnal (Episcopal)", 1916 Hymn 125
S: the oldest copy of this arrangement that I can find is in "Church Hymnal", 1877 hymn 345 attributed to W. Richardson.  It's then in the Scottish Hymnal of 1892 as John Richardson.  I think the first was a misprint. I can't find a composer named W. Richardson in that era.
M: 4/4 % time signature
L: 1/4 % default length
