% 1
[V: S1V1] [Q:1/4=100] B | E F G F/E/ | A G F B | G c =A3/2 A/ | B3 
w: 1.~Lord, as to Thy dear * cross we flee, And plead to be for- giv'n, 
w: 2.~Help us, through good re- * port and ill, Our dai- ly cross to bear: 
w: 3.~Let grace our sel- fish- * ness ex- pel, Our earth- li- ness re- fine; 
w: 4.~If joy shall at Thy * bid- ding fly, And grief's dark day come on, 
w: 5.~Kept peace- ful in the * midst of strife, For- giv- ing and for- giv'n, 
[V: S1V2]  E | E D E D/E/ | D E D F | E E E3/2 E/ | D3 
[V: S2V1]  G, | B, B, B, B, | A, B, B, B, | B, C C3/2 C/ | B,3 
[V: S2V2]  E, | G, F, E, A,/G,/ | F, E, B,, D, | E, C, F,3/2 F,/ | B,,3 
% 5
[V: S1V1] B | e c B c | A A G !sintro!E | A G F F | E3!eintro!|] 
w: So let Thy life our pat- tern be, And form our souls for heav'n. 
w: Like Thee, to do our Fa- ther's will, Our bre- thren's grief to share. 
w: And kind- ness in our bo- soms dwell, As free and true as Thine. 
w: We in our turn would meek- ly cry, "Fa- ther, Thy will be done." 
w: O may we lead the pil- grim's life And fol- low Thee to heav'n. 
[V: S1V2] D | E E E C | C F E E |D E E D | E3 |] 
[V: S2V1] B, | B, A, G, G, | A, B, B, B, | A, B, C B,/A,/ | G,3 |] 
